  "tagline": "Commercial distributed graph database marketed as built natively for ISO GQL.",
  "description": "Ultipa is a commercial property-graph database whose current generation, GQLDB (Ultipa Graph v6), is positioned as a native implementation of ISO/IEC 39075 GQL, alongside its older UQL language. It pairs disk-based native storage with an in-memory graph computing engine for real-time deep traversals and built-in algorithms, and adds vector embeddings and natural-language-to-GQL for RAG. It runs as a single binary, a server or a sharded cluster, and also as Ultipa Cloud. Its full-GQL claim is vendor-stated (earlier v5 conformance docs listed gaps), so test the features you need.",
